ios: missclicks: taps are short and still, the hold menu is tap to pick, slides press only items and scrollbars

A missclick came from a touch meant as a camera turn or a long-press. Now only a short, still touch clicks, and iOS's
own mouse events for a touch are dropped.

- A tap lifts within TAP_MAX_MS (250 ms) of landing, having moved at most TAP_SLOP (8 px, Android's touch slop) along
  either axis. A camera nudge of 8-14 px used to be a tap where it lifted, and the player walked there.
- Early in a touch on the world (within TAP_MAX_MS) the camera turns once the finger passes TAP_SLOP (turnSlop), its
  first step by all the way from where it landed, so a small nudge turns the camera. Later a resting finger may still
  drift up to TOUCH_SLOP (14 px) and its long-press opens the menu.
- The lift point counts: pointerUp takes its screenX/Y (a quick flick's last pointermove can come before it passed the
  slop). A turn follows the finger to the lift point, and a flick that passed the camera's slop only there turns the
  camera by all of it.
- In game, a hold lifted before its menu opened does nothing (it used to left-click: a right click let go a little
  early walked or attacked); so does a long tap where nothing can be chosen (the minimap). A long-press whose timer was
  starved still opens its menu. The title screen is unchanged.
- The hold menu stays open when the finger lifts and an option is picked by tapping it. Lifting never picks (it did
  after a slide onto an option: a camera turn that rested first slid onto the menu beside the finger and picked its
  top option).
- A slide from the side panel, the chat or a window presses where it started only on an item that can be dragged or on
  a scrollbar (slidePresses); elsewhere it pressed a button, a prayer or a dialogue option, and now it does nothing. A
  finger's item drag never does the item's option (objDragByFinger): let go within 5 cycles it ate, wielded or, with
  tap-to-drop, dropped the item.
- hudState().longPressable is false while the finger turns the camera, drags or scrolls, and hudState().touchMoving
  says so (the host's press ring hides then).
- Mouse button events during a touch or within 1 s of one are dropped (GameShell.touchMouseEvent): they are the
  browser's compatibility events for that touch. On the iPhone a quick camera swipe (about 0.3 s) was followed, about
  35 ms after the finger lifted, by a mousedown/mouseup at the swipe's start point, though the surfaces cancel
  touchend: the game took it for a left click and walked there (2 of 7 swipes in a trace). Touches are seen on the
  canvas and surfaces and by a window listener (a finger on a HUD button). A real mouse sends its own pointer events.

